rtunity cost of saving is the lunch you give up by not eating lunch out. The opportunity cost of saving is the Monopoly money you give up by not buying more Monopoly money. The opportunity cost of saving is the phone calls you give up by not making more phone calls. The opportunity cost of saving is the lunch you give up by not having lunch with friends.\nChoices (A), (B), and (C) are all examples of _opportunity costs_. Opportunity costs are the costs of the next best alternative that you give up when you make a choice", "new_cot_probs": [0.0, 0.43131616711616516, 0.28434187173843384, 0.28434187173843384], "cot_prob": [-134.0], "cot_step_prob": [-95.5]}, "2": {"completion": "C). The reason is that the person is willing", "probs": [0.11995488405227661, 0.2539444863796234, 0.36948704719543457, 0.12769131362438202], "prediction": 2, "target_cot_step": "Step 4: This decision will help them save money for their vacation.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: A person wants to start saving money so that they can afford a nice vacation at the end of the year. After looking over their budget and expenses, they decide the best way to save money is to\n\nChoices:\n(A): make more phone calls\n(B): quit eating lunch out\n(C): buy less with monopoly money\n(D): have lunch with friends\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\nStep 1: The person wants to save money for a vacation.\nStep 2: They have looked over their budget and expenses.\nStep 3: They have decided the best way to save money is to quit eating lunch out.", "specificity_preds": [3, 1, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 0, 1, 1, 3, 1, 2, 3, 2, 0, 0, 2], "specificity_probs": [[0.06634528189897537, 0.12394929677248001, 0.10938486456871033, 0.6294664740562439], [0.09701743721961975, 0.5582968592643738, 0.1411595493555069, 0.1599547266960144], [0.10272067040205002, 0.06230323016643524, 0.6698228716850281, 0.11639775335788727], [0.20248650014400482, 0.37829458713531494, 0.25999781489372253, 0.10838321596384048], [0.0160240624